AnimatedDrawings
Source: https://github.com/facebookresearch/AnimatedDrawings
Revision: b859684857519c7424da51a0b0862fbd1fd258f4
Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
Licensed under the MIT License. The complete upstream licence is preserved in
copypaw/vendor/animated_drawings/LICENSE and tests/fixtures/upstream/LICENSE.
Upstream copyright and licence headers are retained in the source files.

Included source: animated_drawings/, including mvc_base_cfg.yaml and shaders.
Included example fixtures: characters/char6/, bvh/fair1/zombie.bvh,
config/motion/zombie.yaml, config/retarget/four_legs.yaml and
config/mvc/four_legs_example.yaml, under tests/fixtures/upstream/.
The fixtures are copied without modification, retaining their upstream paths
relative to examples/ and any embedded notices.

Local modifications:
- Rewrite absolute animated_drawings imports to
  copypaw.vendor.animated_drawings throughout the Python package.
- Replace pkg_resources.resource_filename with importlib.resources.files in
  config.py, utils.py, view/window_view.py and view/mesa_view.py. Resolve the
  base configuration and utility paths from the package root, and shaders from
  view/shaders/ within that package. Preserve utility path search order.
- Replace mutable channel-list defaults in model/bvh.py's BVH_Joint
  constructor and nested frame-channel collector with None, allocating a
  fresh list when omitted.
- Replace the removed NumPy bool8 alias with bool_ in model/arap.py's
  pin-mask declarations, return annotation and array construction, and in
  model/retargeter.py's joint-mask construction.
- Extract the single squared-length product with item() before math.sqrt in
  model/quaternions.py's rotate_between_vectors; NumPy 2 rejects implicit
  conversion of a one-dimensional array to a Python scalar.
- Select the scalar triangle index at [0, 0] before int() in model/arap.py's
  barycentric-coordinate lookup for NumPy 2 compatibility.
- Add an optional control_point_filter callback to AnimatedDrawing.update. When
  set, it receives the BVH frame index and world-space joint positions before
  the ARAP solve, so contact-aware retargeting can adjust paws without changing
  the vendored solver.
- In model/animated_drawing.py's mesh generation, space interior vertices by
  the character's area (about 1000 of them) inside the outline inset by half
  that spacing, and take outline vertices from its corners plus samples at the
  same spacing, dropping any closer than half of it. Upstream used a 40 by 40
  grid over the image and every outline point within a quarter pixel.
- Generate mipmaps for the character texture and sample it with trilinear
  minification, linear magnification and edge clamping.
- When assigning triangles to joints, give a triangle whose centroid lies
  outside the mask the joint of the nearest mask pixel. Upstream gave it the
  last joint in the skeleton.

rtmlib
Source: https://github.com/Tau-J/rtmlib
Version: 0.0.16, from the PyPI wheel rtmlib-0.0.16-py3-none-any.whl
Wheel SHA-256: ba932b25f7d264d7ec4837545c5e7c392001f48b53e22e514cb1497882389eaa
Copyright 2018-2020 Open-MMLab.
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The complete upstream licence
is preserved in copypaw/vendor/rtmlib_onnx/LICENSE, including its copyright notice.
The YOLOX source retains its DWPose attribution and the DARK decoder retains
its easy_ViTPose attribution and paper references.

Included source from rtmlib/tools/: base.py (ONNX inference path),
object_detection/yolox.py, object_detection/post_processings.py (multiclass_nms
and nms), pose_estimation/vitpose.py, pose_estimation/pre_processings.py
(bbox_xyxy2cs, top_down_affine and their affine-transform dependencies), and
pose_estimation/post_processings.py (post_dark_udp).

Local modifications:
- Flatten the subset into copypaw/vendor/rtmlib_onnx/ and rewrite relative
  imports. Rename the processing modules to detection_postprocess.py,
  pose_preprocess.py and pose_postprocess.py. Add a package initializer.
- Restrict BaseTool to ONNX Runtime's CPUExecutionProvider. Remove backend
  selection, accelerator probing, downloads, console output and the abstract
  call interface. Use the model's fixed spatial dimensions when input size is
  omitted, supporting both the 416x416 and 640x640 YOLOX graphs. Request all
  inference outputs directly, retaining contiguous float32 NCHW conversion.
- Restrict YOLOX to raw 80-class output and always return boxes with class IDs.
  Remove human mode, the deprecated mode alias and the embedded-NMS branch
  that cannot provide class IDs. Validate output shape and return float32
  boxes (N, 4) and integer classes (N,), including empty results. Retain the
  upstream decoding, score threshold, class-aware NMS and BGR preprocessing.
- Remove ViTPose's human OpenPose conversion, backend arguments and mutable
  bbox default. Preserve RGB normalization, affine crops and DARK decoding.
- Remove the tensor-to-NumPy conversion in post_dark_udp; ONNX Runtime
  already returns NumPy arrays. Exclude unrelated pose decoders.
- Add adjacent base.pyi, yolox.pyi and vitpose.pyi declarations for the
  inference interfaces used by the capture code and tests.
- Add Apache-2.0 licence pointers and modification notices to the subset.
  Format the retained source and correct the YOLOX output annotation.

